From d4ff050fe3bb0a9b53c4dd6bbdde369a7f4e19fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aleksei Bukhalov <buhaloff.aleks@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 20:23:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] server : add save-on-completion and save-on-shutdown
 prompt-cache triggers

The existing prompt-cache save trigger only fires from the idle-sibling-slot
loop, which requires a second slot to become idle while a different one is
launched. Single-slot sequential traffic (--parallel 1, one growing
conversation per process) never hits it, so the persistent cache never
receives anything to serve.

Add two new triggers that do not depend on a sibling slot:
- save_slot_on_completion(): fires right after a completion finishes,
  debounced per slot via a new --cache-save-ms (default 5000ms, 0 = save
  every completion), gated by a new --cache-save-on-completion /
  --no-cache-save-on-completion flag (default enabled, mirrors
  --cache-idle-slots' own on/off pattern).
- save_slots_on_shutdown(): flushes every slot's current state on graceful
  SIGTERM, bypassing the debounce so a session's last turn is never lost to
  an interval that has not elapsed yet.

Adds two unit tests to the existing cache-trigger test file exercising both
triggers on n_slots=1, and fixes an interaction with the pre-existing
idle-sibling test (isolated via --no-cache-save-on-completion rather than
weakening its assertions).
